P8 deviation (documented, approved 2026-10-15): the release read Qwen3.8-27B's answers from /dev/shm/conseq/short_eval.json, which existed only on the old rig and is gone. It was replaced by a rebuilt stand-in (P8/make_saved.py): the same 240 items, regenerated by the same code with the same seed (the original wordings equal the Claude hand-off, 120 of 120); Qwen3.8-27B reasoning right on every item, as published (100% on both wordings), so the routing rule is exact; the 'Qwen3.8-27B at once' row is dropped because its per-item answers are gone (published: 80.8% / 80.8%).
